# The seed is a byte-for-byte mirror of a live store, not source code.
#
# With core.autocrlf on, git rewrites checked-out JSON to CRLF while the
# application writes LF. `npm run refresh-seed` compares the two by content
# hash, so every run would report the same three databases as changed and
# rewrite them, and git would convert them straight back. Holding the seed
# exactly as stored keeps that comparison meaningful.
seed/** -text
# Run on the Linux VPS; Windows line endings would break bash and Caddy.
*.sh text eol=lf
deploy/Caddyfile text eol=lf
